WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:03.920
WRITTEN BY HYUGA NATSU

01:33.885 --> 01:35.595
THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS.

01:35.678 --> 01:37.305
MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS.

01:45.939 --> 01:46.773
<i>Mother.</i>

01:58.910 --> 02:02.163
<i>Why did Mother have that expression?</i>

02:05.500 --> 02:07.752
Return to your room.

02:14.259 --> 02:16.052
<i>That old man…</i>

02:16.636 --> 02:17.971
<i>That old woman…</i>

02:18.763 --> 02:19.973
<i>Who were they?</i>

02:25.061 --> 02:27.063
<i>I can't remember clearly.</i>

02:38.199 --> 02:39.784
What a terrible dream.

02:47.959 --> 02:50.712
<i>Who were those old people?</i>

02:50.795 --> 02:53.006
<i>At that time, I had no way of knowing.</i>

02:53.089 --> 02:54.465
<i>But later, I was told.</i>

02:55.091 --> 02:58.011
<i>The old man was my father,</i>
<i>and the old woman was my grandmother.</i>

02:58.595 --> 02:59.512
<i>And…</i>

03:00.096 --> 03:02.724
<i>The man I had always thought</i>
<i>was my father,</i>

03:02.807 --> 03:04.017
<i>turned out to be my brother.</i>

03:08.813 --> 03:11.107
<i>Even that slow-witted palace woman</i>

03:11.190 --> 03:12.650
<i>should be realizing it by now.</i>

03:13.818 --> 03:15.069
<i>Or perhaps she already has.</i>

03:16.321 --> 03:18.573
<i>If so, that would be a relief.</i>

03:18.656 --> 03:21.618
<i>I can't stay silent forever.</i>

03:29.709 --> 03:31.920
"Once upon a time, in this land,

03:32.003 --> 03:34.172
another people lived here.

03:34.672 --> 03:37.508
They had no ruler.

03:37.592 --> 03:41.179
But one day, a noble woman
from a distant land arrived,

03:41.262 --> 03:44.015
carrying within her womb
a child of the heavens.

03:44.849 --> 03:48.144
That child became the first emperor
of the Country of Li.

03:48.770 --> 03:52.065
The woman, who could see
even on moonless nights,

03:52.148 --> 03:53.942
came to be called the Wang Mu.

03:54.025 --> 03:57.946
She was even said to be an immortal who
had descended from the celestial realm."

03:58.655 --> 04:01.449
<i>A founding legend of this country, huh?</i>

04:01.532 --> 04:03.076
What do you think, Apothecary?

04:03.159 --> 04:05.578
Lord Jinshi, your face can be seen.

04:07.205 --> 04:09.374
<i>I'm diligently studying here, and yet,</i>

04:09.457 --> 04:13.086
<i>if such a creature is peeking in,</i>
<i>how can I concentrate?</i>

04:13.169 --> 04:14.837
Are there about 20 students?

04:15.880 --> 04:18.383
I thought there would be more…

04:18.466 --> 04:21.344
It started with just ten, so it has grown.

04:21.427 --> 04:25.098
<i>Well, this is about right. That said…</i>

04:25.890 --> 04:28.309
<i>If Lord Jinshi's plan succeeds,</i>

04:28.393 --> 04:30.520
<i>and the literacy rate</i>
<i>of the maids improves,</i>

04:30.603 --> 04:32.939
<i>It could change the very nature</i>
<i>of the rear palace.</i>

04:33.564 --> 04:34.983
<i>In fact, Xiaolan has now</i>

04:35.066 --> 04:39.153
<i>progressed to the stage</i>
<i>where she can read simple stories.</i>

04:39.237 --> 04:42.407
-My lord, it’s about time.
-Yes.

04:43.366 --> 04:44.867
What about you?

04:44.951 --> 04:47.787
I'll stay and observe a little longer.

04:47.870 --> 04:51.291
I see. If anything catches
your attention, report it to me.

04:51.374 --> 04:52.583
Understood.

04:54.085 --> 04:55.295
Xiaolan.

04:56.879 --> 04:58.256
Maomao, you came?

04:58.840 --> 05:01.301
How is it?
Have you learned some characters?

05:02.427 --> 05:04.178
I still have a lot to learn.

05:04.262 --> 05:06.222
I need to ask the teacher something again.

05:06.306 --> 05:08.016
-Maomao, come with me.
-Oh…

05:08.599 --> 05:10.852
The teacher is in the building next door.

05:10.935 --> 05:12.937
I go there sometimes to ask questions.

05:14.480 --> 05:16.566
An old shrine?

05:16.649 --> 05:18.276
Excuse me.

05:18.359 --> 05:20.903
-Sorry to interrupt.
-Coming.

05:21.696 --> 05:24.615
That young lady over there
is a new face, isn't she?

05:32.165 --> 05:35.793
<i>A strangely long and narrow structure</i>
<i>that seems to stretch deep inside.</i>

05:36.627 --> 05:38.463
<i>The pillars are placed closely together.</i>

05:38.546 --> 05:41.215
<i>The rooms must be divided</i>
<i>into very small sections.</i>

05:42.633 --> 05:44.343
Are you curious about that shrine?

05:44.927 --> 05:49.057
Yes, I found its architecture
rather unusual.

05:49.140 --> 05:51.392
That shrine was built by the people

05:51.476 --> 05:53.519
who originally lived in this land.

05:53.603 --> 05:55.938
When Queen Wang Mu
took control of this region,

05:56.022 --> 05:58.566
she did not reject the old faiths.

05:58.649 --> 06:02.320
Is Queen Wang Mu the mother of
the first emperor we just learned about?

06:03.237 --> 06:06.908
Yes. Queen Wang Mu told her son this,

06:07.533 --> 06:09.702
"Anyone who rules this land

06:09.786 --> 06:12.663
must pass through that shrine.

06:12.747 --> 06:15.708
And only those who choose the right path

06:15.792 --> 06:17.668
shall become the ruler of this land."

06:17.752 --> 06:20.296
Her son safely passed through the shrine,

06:20.379 --> 06:22.215
and thus became the emperor.

06:23.007 --> 06:26.761
The reason the capital was relocated to
this place was because of that shrine.

06:26.844 --> 06:27.845
I see!

06:27.929 --> 06:30.932
However, it hasn't been used
for decades now.

06:31.015 --> 06:33.726
Whether it will be used again
in the future, who knows?

06:34.560 --> 06:36.104
What do you mean by that?

06:36.187 --> 06:39.357
The previous emperor’s older brothers

06:39.440 --> 06:41.692
all perished due to a widespread illness.

06:42.735 --> 06:45.238
<i>The only one left was</i>
<i>the previous emperor.</i>

06:45.321 --> 06:48.950
<i>So the decision was made without</i>
<i>the need for the passage ritual.</i>

06:49.617 --> 06:52.995
I'm glad to see someone
interested in that place.

06:53.079 --> 06:55.289
It's been quite some time
since that happened.

06:55.373 --> 06:58.292
Were there people who used to take
an interest in it before?

06:58.376 --> 06:59.210
Yes.

06:59.293 --> 07:02.380
There used to be a rather unique
court physician here.

07:02.463 --> 07:06.300
Whenever he had free time,
he would wander around the rear palace.

07:06.384 --> 07:09.053
Just like you, he was also curious
about that shrine…

07:09.137 --> 07:11.806
-Wait, could it be Luomen?
-Oh? You know him?

07:12.390 --> 07:14.475
<i>Damn, I let that slip.</i>

07:14.976 --> 07:16.060
He was my foster father.

07:16.144 --> 07:19.897
After leaving the rear palace, he ran
an apothecary in the pleasure district.

07:19.981 --> 07:22.400
I see, so you're Luomen's…

07:23.359 --> 07:26.863
<i>Was this man close to my father?</i>

07:26.946 --> 07:27.780
Maomao!

07:28.448 --> 07:29.949
Look! I wrote it!

07:30.575 --> 07:31.659
Oh!

07:34.245 --> 07:35.663
There is no poison.

07:37.707 --> 07:40.418
-I'll take my leave.
-Wait, Apothecary.

07:41.002 --> 07:43.838
After this, I want you to accompany me.

07:44.547 --> 07:45.423
Where to?

07:45.506 --> 07:47.633
To the Shrine of Choosing.

07:49.844 --> 07:52.013
Why all of a sudden?

07:52.096 --> 07:54.765
<i>What exactly is he planning to do?</i>

07:55.850 --> 07:57.518
<i>It's the old shrine I saw during the day.</i>

07:58.644 --> 07:59.604
<i>And also…</i>

07:59.687 --> 08:01.772
<i>the teacher at the learning hall?</i>

08:01.856 --> 08:03.566
I have been expecting you.

08:03.649 --> 08:06.736
May I pass through it once more?

08:06.819 --> 08:09.906
No matter how many times you come,
it may not change anything,

08:09.989 --> 08:11.282
but if you are still willing to…

08:11.908 --> 08:15.161
<i>That’s quite a daring way</i>
<i>to speak to the Emperor.</i>

08:15.244 --> 08:16.871
Who will accompany you?

08:17.955 --> 08:19.457
Then, these two.

08:19.540 --> 08:20.625
What?!

08:20.708 --> 08:23.419
Isn’t this place off-limits to women?

08:24.587 --> 08:26.881
The Queen Wang Mu and the Empress Dowager
were both women, you know.

08:28.090 --> 08:30.635
-Please, come on in.
-Well then, shall we proceed?

08:36.641 --> 08:38.267
<i>Three doors?</i>

08:39.268 --> 08:42.146
<i>"Do not pass through the red door"?</i>

08:42.230 --> 08:43.147
<i>The doors are…</i>

08:43.231 --> 08:45.650
<i>blue, red, and green.</i>

08:46.275 --> 08:48.528
<i>So we’re supposed to choose</i>
<i>either blue or green?</i>

08:48.611 --> 08:51.113
Which door will you choose?

08:51.197 --> 08:54.659
I’ll go with blue this time.
Last time, I chose green.

08:54.742 --> 08:56.577
Indeed, that was the case.

08:56.661 --> 08:58.454
Well then, this way.

09:01.999 --> 09:05.419
Please consider those of us
who manage this place.

09:05.503 --> 09:08.130
Just when we think it is no longer in use,

09:08.214 --> 09:10.716
someone suddenly shows up.

09:11.551 --> 09:12.677
I have caused you trouble.

09:14.679 --> 09:16.764
<i>Three doors again…</i>

09:16.847 --> 09:19.600
<i>Green, brown, and light blue.</i>
<i>Next it says,</i>

09:20.184 --> 09:21.978
<i>"Do not pass through the brown door."</i>

09:22.061 --> 09:24.021
I’ll choose green.

09:24.105 --> 09:25.106
<i>No way…</i>

09:27.191 --> 09:28.568
<i>Will this just keep</i>

09:28.651 --> 09:30.653
<i>repeating forever?</i>

09:36.200 --> 09:39.328
<i>Going up, going down,</i>
<i>going back, turning around…</i>

09:39.412 --> 09:41.747
<i>I’ve completely lost</i>
<i>my sense of direction.</i>

09:41.831 --> 09:44.917
<i>It feels like we’re just going</i>
<i>around in circles.</i>

09:45.418 --> 09:48.296
<i>Why did the Emperor bring me here?</i>

09:49.589 --> 09:51.757
<i>I wish this would end soon.</i>

09:56.929 --> 09:58.472
This is the final door.

09:59.599 --> 10:00.725
<i>The next set of doors are…</i>

10:00.808 --> 10:03.644
<i>blue, purple, and yellow. And it says,</i>

10:04.186 --> 10:06.606
<i>"Do not pass through the blue door."</i>

10:07.565 --> 10:11.235
<i>Also, there’s another door leading here.</i>

10:11.319 --> 10:13.946
<i>Does that mean there's another path</i>
<i>that merges here?</i>

10:14.030 --> 10:15.364
I’ve decided.

10:16.240 --> 10:17.074
I’ll choose yellow.

10:19.910 --> 10:22.204
-Are you sure?
-Yes.

10:25.833 --> 10:27.126
<i>A dead end?</i>

10:28.002 --> 10:31.130
<i>"Child of royalty,</i>
<i>yet not child of the Wang Mu."</i>

10:31.839 --> 10:35.051
<i>I don’t understand the meaning,</i>
<i>but it’s clearly a rejection.</i>

10:35.134 --> 10:37.428
It's the same result as last time.

10:42.391 --> 10:45.019
<i>He looks unusually serious.</i>

10:45.102 --> 10:48.272
Is it impossible for me
to know the will of heaven?

10:48.356 --> 10:50.524
What are you saying?

10:50.608 --> 10:53.986
Ever since this shrine was sealed
within the rear palace,

10:54.070 --> 10:57.698
I have been the only one
left to manage it.

10:57.782 --> 11:00.284
What meaning could
the will of heaven possibly have?

11:00.368 --> 11:02.578
<i>This old eunuch was probably</i>

11:02.662 --> 11:04.413
<i>managing this shrine long before</i>

11:04.997 --> 11:07.166
<i>the rear palace was even established.</i>

11:07.750 --> 11:09.293
<i>In order to continue maintaining it,</i>

11:09.377 --> 11:12.004
<i>he went so far as to become a eunuch</i>
<i>just so he could stay here.</i>

11:13.881 --> 11:15.883
Your way out is over there.

11:21.138 --> 11:24.225
<i>The Emperor followed</i>
<i>the instructions on the signs.</i>

11:24.308 --> 11:26.519
<i>There shouldn’t have been any mistakes.</i>

11:26.602 --> 11:28.938
<i>And yet, he still didn’t</i>
<i>reach the right answer.</i>

11:30.106 --> 11:32.316
<i>Was there another meaning behind all that?</i>

11:32.817 --> 11:34.318
<i>The number of rooms?</i>

11:34.402 --> 11:36.028
<i>The colors of the doors chosen?</i>

11:36.112 --> 11:39.740
I'm sure Luomen would know.

11:39.824 --> 11:41.784
<i>My old man would know?</i>

11:41.867 --> 11:44.161
Are you saying that my father
would be able to figure it out?

11:44.245 --> 11:46.414
Well, who knows?

11:47.248 --> 11:49.625
<i>My father's knowledge</i>
<i>is certainly incredible.</i>

11:50.459 --> 11:53.796
<i>But being told, "This is beyond you,"</i>
<i>really pisses me off.</i>

11:54.547 --> 11:58.717
<i>My father's knowledge is exceptional,</i>
<i>especially when it comes to medicine.</i>

11:58.801 --> 12:00.678
<i>Does that mean this is related to that?</i>

12:10.062 --> 12:12.481
<i>Three doors, three colors…</i>

12:13.315 --> 12:16.777
<i>"Child of royalty,</i>
<i>yet not child of the Wang Mu."</i>

12:16.861 --> 12:20.030
<i>What is the true meaning</i>
<i>behind those words?</i>

12:24.785 --> 12:26.954
Do you understand the meaning of

12:27.037 --> 12:28.581
"Yet not the child of the Wang Mu"?

12:29.582 --> 12:30.458
<i>Now that I think about it…</i>

12:31.083 --> 12:33.461
<i>In the story of</i>
<i>the founding of the nation,</i>

12:33.544 --> 12:36.338
<i>it’s always the first emperor's mother,</i>
<i>Queen Wang Mu, who appears.</i>

12:36.422 --> 12:37.882
<i>The father is never spoken of.</i>

12:38.382 --> 12:41.719
<i>Then one would expect</i>
<i>the maternal lineage to be valued,</i>

12:41.802 --> 12:45.681
<i>yet in reality,</i>
<i>succession is passed down through males.</i>

12:45.764 --> 12:49.226
<i>If they intended to preserve</i>
<i>Queen Wang Mu's bloodline…</i>

12:49.310 --> 12:51.520
The previous emperor’s older brothers

12:51.604 --> 12:54.523
all perished due to a widespread illness.

12:54.607 --> 12:55.649
Lord Jinshi.

12:56.150 --> 12:58.194
Have you realized something?

12:58.277 --> 13:01.655
Were the former emperor’s brothers
full siblings?

13:02.156 --> 13:04.033
Not all of them,

13:04.116 --> 13:07.620
but I heard that the mothers of
the imperial princes were sisters.

13:07.703 --> 13:10.706
In other words,
their blood was quite close.

13:12.082 --> 13:14.543
This may sound rude,

13:14.627 --> 13:16.378
but may I ask you something?

13:16.462 --> 13:18.047
I permit it. Speak.

13:19.131 --> 13:22.009
Throughout generations,

13:22.092 --> 13:25.012
haven’t many of the emperors
had poor eyesight?

13:27.223 --> 13:30.726
I have heard that their eyesight
certainly wasn’t very good.

13:30.809 --> 13:32.978
But the previous emperor had good vision.

13:33.479 --> 13:34.688
<i>I knew it.</i>

13:35.272 --> 13:38.359
Is it possible to pass through
that shrine once more?

13:39.026 --> 13:42.071
Does the young lady have
the qualifications for that?

13:43.197 --> 13:45.074
You brought her along with you earlier,

13:45.157 --> 13:47.243
but entering multiple times
is not a good idea.

13:47.910 --> 13:51.914
Especially if she intends to interfere
with the choice of doors.

13:51.997 --> 13:55.251
Besides, she’s neither a consort
nor a princess, is she?

13:55.834 --> 13:57.711
<i>I'm just a mere servant girl.</i>

13:58.712 --> 14:01.298
Then shall I elevate her to a consort?

14:01.382 --> 14:04.009
Though convincing Lakan
will be troublesome.

14:04.885 --> 14:07.221
<i>-He must be joking.</i>
-You must be joking!

14:07.304 --> 14:09.098
What would the other consorts think?

14:10.849 --> 14:13.269
That is true. In that case,

14:13.352 --> 14:15.271
would you take her instead?

14:17.064 --> 14:18.691
That would be acceptable, wouldn’t it?

14:18.774 --> 14:21.485
If that is His Majesty’s wish.

14:22.194 --> 14:23.821
Then, shall we go?

14:24.989 --> 14:27.199
<i>He seems more playful than usual.</i>

14:29.076 --> 14:32.580
<i>First, the blue, red, and green doors.</i>

14:33.205 --> 14:35.332
<i>"Do not pass through the red door."</i>

14:35.416 --> 14:37.835
-Which will you choose?
-The blue one.

14:38.586 --> 14:41.755
<i>This is the same</i>
<i>as the one His Majesty chose.</i>

14:43.424 --> 14:46.802
Next, there's green, brown,
and light blue. It says,

14:46.886 --> 14:48.304
"Do not pass through the brown door."

14:49.471 --> 14:50.598
The light blue door.

14:54.018 --> 14:56.228
The one I chose is different from yours.

14:57.813 --> 15:00.983
<i>When I passed through earlier,</i>
<i>I didn't realize it.</i>

15:01.066 --> 15:02.985
<i>If there is a door that only</i>
<i>a "child of Wang Mu" can choose…</i>

15:04.820 --> 15:08.073
<i>Then the key must lie</i>
<i>in the "color" of the doors.</i>

15:10.993 --> 15:12.953
<i>This is the tenth one.</i>

15:13.037 --> 15:15.497
<i>There's a white, purple, and green door.</i>

15:16.332 --> 15:18.459
<i>It says, "Pass through the red door."</i>

15:20.336 --> 15:23.339
But there is no red door.
What does this mean?

15:23.964 --> 15:25.341
The green door.

15:26.300 --> 15:27.343
Green?

15:28.677 --> 15:29.762
You’ll know once you go through.

15:33.349 --> 15:34.475
<i>This is…?</i>

15:40.689 --> 15:42.524
Congratulations.

15:42.608 --> 15:44.777
It seems you have chosen the correct path.

15:45.861 --> 15:48.489
Long ago, those chosen by Queen Wang Mu

15:48.572 --> 15:50.824
became the next king.

15:50.908 --> 15:52.826
They would stand here

15:52.910 --> 15:55.829
<i>and swear an oath to the people.</i>

15:55.913 --> 15:59.291
<i>If no one could choose this path,</i>

15:59.375 --> 16:02.628
<i>they would return to this shrine</i>

16:02.711 --> 16:05.381
<i>with a consort who could.</i>

16:05.881 --> 16:09.051
Originally, one who inherited
the rightful blood

16:09.134 --> 16:11.053
was meant to do it.

16:11.136 --> 16:12.721
But this time,

16:12.805 --> 16:15.349
it seems that someone else
has found the answer.

16:15.975 --> 16:18.268
<i>You're the one who provoked me!</i>

16:18.352 --> 16:19.436
<i>What is this guy's problem?</i>

16:19.520 --> 16:22.189
More importantly, explain this to me

16:22.272 --> 16:25.109
in a way Jinshi can understand.

16:25.192 --> 16:26.151
Perhaps

16:26.235 --> 16:29.071
you should ask the young lady over there.

16:29.989 --> 16:30.990
<i>This guy…</i>

16:31.073 --> 16:33.367
<i>Is he trying to make me explain?</i>

16:33.450 --> 16:34.743
So it seems.

16:38.205 --> 16:41.125
In the founding legend,
it is said that Queen Wang Mu

16:41.208 --> 16:45.004
possessed eyes that could
see through darkness.

16:45.546 --> 16:47.256
Those chosen by this shrine…

16:47.339 --> 16:49.633
In other words, those who carry
Queen Wang Mu's blood

16:49.717 --> 16:53.387
are said to have eyes
that cannot distinguish colors.

16:53.971 --> 16:55.347
Eyes that cannot distinguish colors?

16:56.015 --> 16:57.057
What do you mean?

16:57.725 --> 17:00.352
Then, allow me to explain the logic

17:00.436 --> 17:02.187
by which I chose the doors earlier.

17:02.771 --> 17:05.691
<i>At first, there were three doors.</i>
<i>Blue, red, and green.</i>

17:06.442 --> 17:08.694
<i>The instruction was</i>
<i>"Do not pass through the red door."</i>

17:09.278 --> 17:12.489
<i>That means both blue and green</i>
<i>should be correct choices,</i>

17:12.573 --> 17:13.449
<i>but "the child of Wang Mu"</i>

17:13.532 --> 17:15.868
<i>would have chosen blue.</i>

17:15.951 --> 17:19.371
<i>Because if one cannot distinguish</i>
<i>between red and green,</i>

17:19.455 --> 17:21.957
<i>they would choose the door</i>
<i>that is definitely not red.</i>

17:22.666 --> 17:25.669
Unable to distinguish red from green?

17:25.753 --> 17:27.755
It is rare in this country,

17:27.838 --> 17:31.341
but in the western lands, it is said that

17:31.425 --> 17:33.969
one in ten men cannot differentiate
between red and green.

17:34.053 --> 17:36.346
Luomen would know that, wouldn't he?

17:36.972 --> 17:39.391
<i>My father, who studied abroad</i>
<i>in the western lands,</i>

17:39.475 --> 17:41.101
<i>would have known this trait.</i>

17:41.852 --> 17:43.979
<i>So that's what he meant by that.</i>

17:44.563 --> 17:45.939
The next door followed the same logic.

17:46.648 --> 17:48.275
<i>It said,</i>
<i>"Do not pass through the brown door."</i>

17:48.984 --> 17:51.361
<i>If one cannot distinguish</i>
<i>between brown and green,</i>

17:51.445 --> 17:53.781
<i>then by process of elimination,</i>
<i>they'd choose the light blue door.</i>

17:54.406 --> 17:55.449
For the final door,

17:55.532 --> 17:57.826
<i>the instruction was</i>
<i>"Pass through the red door."</i>

17:57.910 --> 18:01.080
<i>However, there was no red door.</i>

18:01.997 --> 18:05.793
<i>But if one could clearly distinguish</i>
<i>between white and purple,</i>

18:05.876 --> 18:08.337
<i>then the remaining door must be red.</i>

18:08.962 --> 18:12.049
In other words, while it appeared
as though there were two correct choices,

18:12.758 --> 18:16.303
<i>the correct choice was only one.</i>

18:16.386 --> 18:17.805
But

18:17.888 --> 18:20.516
if every emperor throughout history
had such a trait,

18:20.599 --> 18:22.601
someone would notice, don't you think?

18:22.684 --> 18:25.104
My foster father once told me that

18:25.187 --> 18:26.897
even if one cannot distinguish colors,

18:26.980 --> 18:29.608
they can learn to adapt over time.

18:29.691 --> 18:32.319
So people around them
might not even notice.

18:32.402 --> 18:35.572
And, in exchange for
their difficulty with color perception,

18:35.656 --> 18:37.449
they are said to have
excellent night vision.

18:37.950 --> 18:39.701
That might be the origin of the legend

18:39.785 --> 18:41.662
about the eyes of Queen Wang Mu.

18:42.162 --> 18:45.040
So only those who inherit this trait
from Queen Wang Mu

18:45.124 --> 18:47.626
can pass through this place?

18:47.709 --> 18:51.296
Perhaps some people have stumbled
through by chance,

18:51.797 --> 18:53.882
but the probability of making it
to the final chamber

18:53.966 --> 18:55.551
would be incredibly low.

18:56.844 --> 18:58.178
<i>In the old tales,</i>

18:58.262 --> 19:01.640
<i>it is said that Queen Wang Mu</i>
<i>came from a distant land.</i>

19:02.766 --> 19:06.687
<i>She had the trait of being</i>
<i>unable to distinguish colors,</i>

19:06.770 --> 19:08.147
<i>yet she came from the western lands</i>

19:08.230 --> 19:10.816
<i>with her attendants to this land.</i>

19:10.899 --> 19:13.110
Settling in a new land

19:13.193 --> 19:15.195
wasn't an easy task.

19:15.279 --> 19:17.489
So, she married the leader

19:17.573 --> 19:19.032
of this land.

19:19.116 --> 19:20.826
Wait, Apothecary.

19:20.909 --> 19:23.871
In the legends, it is said that
Queen Wang Mu had no husband.

19:23.954 --> 19:26.874
That is what makes
Queen Wang Mu so cunning.

19:27.875 --> 19:29.585
<i>To prevent the bloodline</i>
<i>from becoming concentrated,</i>

19:29.668 --> 19:31.503
<i>it was not uncommon</i>

19:31.587 --> 19:33.130
<i>to marry someone from outside.</i>

19:33.755 --> 19:35.257
Although Queen Wang Mu is the ancestor,

19:35.340 --> 19:38.093
the throne has been
passed down by male heirs

19:38.177 --> 19:40.053
because they followed
the method of establishing

19:40.137 --> 19:42.306
the leader of the bloodline.

19:42.389 --> 19:44.933
However, Queen Wang Mu's descendants

19:45.017 --> 19:47.311
couldn't accept the idea
of their blood thinning out

19:47.394 --> 19:49.396
and disappearing entirely.

19:50.063 --> 19:51.940
<i>A way to ensure that Queen Wang Mu's blood</i>

19:52.024 --> 19:53.400
<i>will be preserved for future generations…</i>

19:53.483 --> 19:56.153
That is the "Shrine of Choosing."

19:57.279 --> 20:00.073
<i>If no one possesses the trait,</i>

20:00.157 --> 20:03.535
<i>then someone of close blood to</i>
<i>Queen Wang Mu is taken as consort,</i>

20:03.619 --> 20:04.661
<i>and together, they enter the shrine.</i>

20:05.704 --> 20:07.706
<i>The reason why consorts are also allowed</i>

20:07.789 --> 20:09.374
<i>to enter the shrine is because of this.</i>

20:09.458 --> 20:11.251
<i>Bit by bit, in this manner,</i>

20:11.335 --> 20:13.545
<i>they embedded themselves</i>
<i>at the heart of the nation,</i>

20:14.254 --> 20:17.466
<i>erasing the existence of</i>
<i>the original rulers from the stories</i>

20:17.549 --> 20:19.259
<i>until only Queen Wang Mu</i>
<i>remained as the true ancestor.</i>

20:20.010 --> 20:22.429
<i>In time, as those who remembered</i>
<i>the past disappeared,</i>

20:22.512 --> 20:24.932
<i>the only remaining story became the truth.</i>

20:25.432 --> 20:27.851
<i>It was an extremely peaceful yet…</i>

20:27.935 --> 20:29.686
<i>slow shift of power.</i>

20:29.770 --> 20:32.856
<i>Well, of course, that’s not something</i>
<i>I can say right now.</i>

20:32.940 --> 20:34.316
So, does that mean

20:34.399 --> 20:36.944
I do not carry the blood of Queen Wang Mu?

20:37.527 --> 20:41.531
The existence of this shrine is
the only definitive way to determine that.

20:41.615 --> 20:43.742
Even if a parent possesses the trait,

20:43.825 --> 20:45.786
it does not always
pass down to their children.

20:46.286 --> 20:50.040
Also, when blood becomes too concentrated,
it can cause adverse effects.

20:50.123 --> 20:53.126
It is possible that
the late emperor’s siblings

20:53.210 --> 20:55.003
fell ill for that very reason.

20:56.129 --> 20:58.257
To think that a mere girl

20:58.340 --> 21:01.468
would actually solve the mystery
is something I never expected.

21:01.969 --> 21:03.178
<i>"Mere girl"?</i>

21:03.262 --> 21:05.639
It is said that Queen Wang Mu

21:05.722 --> 21:07.641
was able to rule this land because of

21:07.724 --> 21:09.851
her exceptional wisdom.

21:09.935 --> 21:12.437
If you're going to dilute
the bloodline at this point,

21:12.521 --> 21:15.399
why not incorporate someone like her?

21:17.776 --> 21:20.195
<i>What nonsense is that old guy saying?</i>

21:20.279 --> 21:22.072
Well, that might be interesting,

21:22.155 --> 21:25.200
but I’d rather not make an enemy
of Lakan, and more importantly,

21:25.284 --> 21:27.995
she’s lacking about
15 centimeters around the chest.

21:28.495 --> 21:29.746
<i>Mind your own business.</i>

21:30.414 --> 21:32.249
But do be careful.

21:32.332 --> 21:33.834
There are many who would not

21:33.917 --> 21:36.962
welcome the introduction of outside blood.

21:37.045 --> 21:38.463
I am well aware of that.

21:38.547 --> 21:42.092
Does Your Majesty truly understand?

21:42.968 --> 21:44.845
Please be careful.

21:47.264 --> 21:48.557
Understood.

21:58.984 --> 22:00.986
<i>Who is he really?</i>

22:01.945 --> 22:04.531
<i>Just the Emperor’s favored eunuch?</i>

22:04.614 --> 22:07.242
<i>Is that really all?</i>

22:09.995 --> 22:11.330
<i>It doesn't matter.</i>

22:11.913 --> 22:13.332
<i>Ignorance is bliss.</i>

22:14.124 --> 22:15.459
<i>That's just how it is.</i>

23:46.091 --> 23:50.262
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:57.394 --> 24:00.397
<i>Next episode, "Empress Dowager."</i>

24:00.480 --> 24:01.898
